1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,897
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,937
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:27,667
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,517
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:40,877
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, it's so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,857
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:55,677
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,020
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,577
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:08,877
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,520
Believe in wonderland.

17
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,557
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary life.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,717
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,480
We live in one another.

26
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:56,917
Nami, how you feeling?

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,235
Are you completely recovered
from your illness already?

28
00:02:00,700 --> 00:02:02,480
Sure am. I feel great.

29
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,130
Hey!

30
00:02:04,213 --> 00:02:05,917
How about we go say
goodbye to the old doctor

31
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,837
lady and that Dalton guy from the village?

32
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:08,937
Don't be so thoughtless.

33
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:10,557
We need to leave Chopper alone with Dr.

34
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:11,470
E for a while.

35
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:13,462
He lived with her for six years.

36
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:15,257
We should let them say goodbye in peace.

37
00:02:15,340 --> 00:02:17,757
I'm sure it's going to be
really sad for them both.

38
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:18,670
Dr.

39
00:02:18,753 --> 00:02:23,341
E acts all tough in front of us, but deep
down, I think she really is a kind person.

40
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,390
You sure?

41
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:28,177
So we're just going to leave
without saying anything to her?

42
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:29,277
Yeah, that's right.

43
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,437
Once Chopper comes back,

44
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:34,108
we'll go straight down the
mountain and set sail to Alabasta.

45
00:02:34,280 --> 00:02:36,162
Sounds good to you, right, Vivi?

46
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:39,217
Yes, now that we have a
doctor coming with us.

47
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:40,130
Doctor?

48
00:02:40,213 --> 00:02:43,457
Well, in that case, I'll go
ahead and get the ropeway ready.

49
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:45,360
Hey, Luffy, give me a hand!

50
00:02:45,540 --> 00:02:47,834
I didn't even know there was a ropeway!

51
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,100
So cool!

52
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:01,560
Well, look at that.

53
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:04,337
It seems as if we have a
couple of patients missing.

54
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:05,660
Yes, they all left.

55
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,762
Directly disobeying your orders.

56
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:10,600
Oh, I see.

57
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:12,860
What am I going to do with them?

58
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,160
Dr. Ane!

59
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:28,730
Doctorine!

60
00:03:28,813 --> 00:03:30,240
I need to talk to you right now.

61
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,997
Chopper, where have you been all day?

62
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:34,557
Hurry up and get downstairs.

63
00:03:34,640 --> 00:03:37,037
You can help the men
take the cannons outside.

64
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:38,557
Please listen, Doctorine.

65
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,277
I'm going to become a pirate.

66
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:42,297
I'm leaving with the others right now.

67
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:43,500
What did you say?

68
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:44,935
I'm going out to sea.

69
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,557
I'm coming on board with
them as the ship's doctor.

70
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:49,397
I'm going to travel everywhere.

71
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,320
Stop this foolishness, Chopper!

72
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:55,317
Now listen, you know
you're my only assistant?

73
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:58,497
I'm the one who taught you
everything you know about medicine!

74
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:02,260
Do you really feel no gratitude
at all for what I've done?

75
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,297
No, no, that isn't true.

76
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:06,757
I'm incredibly grateful to you, Doctorine.

77
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,937
And I'll always love this land.

78
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:11,237
It's where I met you
and Doctor, after all.

79
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,797
Then you can just stay here.

80
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,617
If you think you can find
another home as nice as this one.

81
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:19,177
Somewhere in the outside
world, you're sadly mistaken.

82
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:21,717
Those pirates aren't good
for anything, Chopper.

83
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,797
You'll end up dead on some
vagabond sword in no time.

84
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:25,939
I can accept that.

85
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:29,182
Don't sound so sure of yourself.

86
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:32,857
A reindeer going out to sea, that's the
most ridiculous thing I've ever heard of.

87
00:04:32,940 --> 00:04:34,234
Yeah, I am a reindeer.

88
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:36,320
But still, I'm a man.

89
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:46,357
You can talk tough for now, but
you're still my assistant, Chopper.

90
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:49,377
If you want to leave, you're going
to have to go through me first.

91
00:04:49,460 --> 00:04:50,519
Do you understand?

92
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:52,940
Dr. Eam...

93
00:04:56,200 --> 00:05:00,297
You're still afraid of your own shadow,
and you're telling me you're a man?

94
00:05:00,380 --> 00:05:02,440
Oh, please, don't make me laugh.

95
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:03,870
Dr.

96
00:05:03,953 --> 00:05:06,120
Eam, these pirates, don't you see?

97
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:07,380
Shut up!

98
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:08,660
Let's go!

99
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,060
They like me.

100
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:13,460
Quiet, you!

101
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:16,370
No!

102
00:05:16,453 --> 00:05:18,220
I'm not going to let you leave me!

103
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:23,740
You're staying!

104
00:05:26,340 --> 00:05:28,140
Get back here, chopper!

105
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,140
You can't escape!

106
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,677
I wonder what all that noise is about.

107
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:37,590
Who knows?

108
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:41,077
Whatever's going on, we'd better
hurry and get all this stuff outside.

109
00:05:41,160 --> 00:05:42,477
If we aren't careful, Dr.

110
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:45,325
Karoo will start using
us for target practice.

111
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:47,400
Don't exaggerate. Come back!

112
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,271
I won't let you get away from me, chopper!

113
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,480
Get away!

114
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:57,381
What's going on?

115
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:59,537
There's a lot of noise
coming from the castle.

116
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:03,597
Go and consider it, making all that noise
when those two are trying to say goodbye.

117
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,268
That's just downright rude.

118
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:08,860
I'm sorry, Dr.

119
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:12,548
E, but I want to go out and see
the world beyond this island.

120
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:20,757
Why could someone like you
do on a pirate ship, Chopper?

121
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:24,487
Are you going to try to live
some fantasy like that old quack?

122
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:27,080
No, you're wrong!

123
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,720
It wasn't a fantasy!

124
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:32,475
Doctor's research was finally
completed before he died!

125
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,760
Oh, finally, here he comes. Huh?

126
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:36,970
Huh?

127
00:06:37,053 --> 00:06:37,883
What's going on?

128
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:39,420
He's being chased!

129
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,350
Hey!

130
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:43,264
We got the ropeway ready to go!

131
00:06:44,940 --> 00:06:46,397
Everyone, get on the sleigh!

132
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,937
We're going to head down the mountain!

133
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:48,850
Hurry!

134
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,840
Hey, look at that!

135
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,707
What the hell is that thing?

136
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,480
That's the witch's sleigh.

137
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:00,700
What was that thing?

138
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,019
It looked like Dr.

139
00:08:02,120 --> 00:08:02,950
Correa's reindeer.

140
00:08:03,033 --> 00:08:05,317
Then those pirates were
riding in the sleigh.

141
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,117
What's going on up there anyway?

142
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,517
What happened to Wapol?

143
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,071
I hope Dalton's all right

144
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:16,040
That was fun!

145
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:18,237
Hey reindeer, can we do that again?

146
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:20,517
You idiot, we don't have time for that.

147
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,160
I thought I was gonna die Hey, where am I?

148
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,261
What's going on?

149
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:27,120
Oh Sanji, you're awake. You okay?

150
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,176
You really think that was
the best way to say goodbye?

151
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:41,020
A pet I was taking care of is being
looked after by someone else now.

152
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:42,370
That's all.

153
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:48,100
Besides, I don't like long goodbyes.

154
00:08:54,600 --> 00:09:00,500
Come on We have work to do We have to
prepare a fitting send-off It hurts

155
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:07,497
I've finally done it This is it
This reaction I've been waiting

156
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:12,660
30 years for this Doctor It wasn't
a fantasy like she said, right?

157
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:13,997
You finished your work.

158
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,727
You accomplished your dream.

159
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:18,700
But was that all a lie, too?

160
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,080
I've done it, Chopper!

161
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:23,100
My research is a success!

162
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:27,017
Did you lie because you knew how sad I'd
be if you died without completing it?

163
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:30,357
Nothing is impossible for a
man who raises a pirate flag!

164
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,220
Please say it again, Doctor!

165
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:39,220
All right, young man, are you ready?

166
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,570
Yes!

167
00:09:40,653 --> 00:09:41,483
Then fire!

168
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,155
Listen to me, Kureha.

169
00:09:43,360 --> 00:09:45,080
This dust is special.

170
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,740
Sleep! Sleep! Sleep!

171
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:50,390
Dr.

172
00:09:50,473 --> 00:09:52,040
Corgi, what are you doing?

173
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,660
Just chat up and watch.

174
00:09:59,420 --> 00:10:01,067
It's coming from the castle!

175
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,497
Is Waffle setting off
fireworks or something?

176
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,177
No, those are cannon blasts!

177
00:10:05,260 --> 00:10:06,217
What's happening up there?

178
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:07,660
Watch for cannonballs!

179
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:10,717
It's too dark to see what
they're doing up there!

180
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,630
Dr.

181
00:10:11,713 --> 00:10:13,297
Corgi, all the cannons have been fired!

182
00:10:13,380 --> 00:10:14,540
Then light them up!

183
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:17,090
Look!

184
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:27,120
Oh, cool.

185
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:30,350
Wow.

186
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:38,357
After 30 years, this just finally
completes my research. This is...

187
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:40,520
this is just absolutely amazing.

188
00:10:42,680 --> 00:10:45,117
I still can't understand
what that idiot was thinking.

189
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:48,560
I will make cherry blossoms
bloom in this country.

190
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:52,704
Once my invention is perfected,
this country is as good as saved.

191
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,500
Get out of here, you crazy quack!

192
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:57,836
I thought lizard eyeballs would work!

193
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:03,100
This is no ordinary red dust, Pereja.

194
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,737
This dust is designed
to attach itself to the

195
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:08,337
white snowflakes as they
come down from the sky.

196
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:13,008
The white snow will then become a beautiful
shade of pink for everyone to see.

197
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:20,580
Doctor!

198
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,477
Doctor Eve!

199
00:11:23,560 --> 00:11:26,760
Oh, my God.

200
00:11:58,260 --> 00:12:01,025
I promise you, I'm not
going to shoot you, see?

201
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:04,020
My name is Hiriluk, Dr. Hiriluk.

202
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,840
Tony, Tony Chopper.

203
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:07,862
Cool name, huh?

204
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:10,731
Anyway, that's what I'm going to call you.

205
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:13,075
You're going to become a great doctor.

206
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:14,720
I'll make sure of it.

207
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:24,477
Even if I should disappear right
now, my dream will come true.

208
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:27,560
I've had a marvelous life.

209
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,620
Thank you so much, Chopper!

210
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:48,840
Now, have a safe trip, my stupid son.

211
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,878
And these cherry blossoms
are like party decorations.

212
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,837
Come on, Chopper, step out of it.

213
00:13:05,920 --> 00:13:09,317
You can't just sit there and
daze all night long, you know.

214
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,400
You want a drink?

215
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:12,840
Come sing a song with us.

216
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:16,640
Here, shove these chopsticks
up your nose. Go on.

217
00:13:17,020 --> 00:13:18,457
There's a great moonlit night.

218
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:19,937
Cherry blossoms are in the air.

219
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:21,255
How did we not party?

220
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,899
They're a handful.

221
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:28,394
I hate to tell you, but your new
friends are about as crazy as they come.

222
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:31,780
My friends? That's right.

223
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:33,897
These guys can really be a lot to handle,

224
00:13:33,980 --> 00:13:37,577
but now that you're one of us, you're
going to have to get used to it.

225
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:38,740
Yes! Come on!

226
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:43,159
Conney, what in the world were you
doing frozen in the river like that?

227
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:47,577
That bird, Ten Berries, says he
slipped and fell into the river.

228
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,697
He's a clumsy one.

229
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:50,120
Be quiet, Mr. Bushido.

230
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:52,380
Huh? Yeah?

231
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,537
He said that the guy named Zoro was
swimming in the river and disappeared.

232
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:57,037
He thought Zoro was in trouble,

233
00:13:57,120 --> 00:14:00,017
so he jumped into the river to help
and ended up getting frozen in it.

234
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:01,629
So this is all your fault!

235
00:14:02,520 --> 00:14:05,837
So you were really able to understand
everything Kari was saying?

236
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:06,750
Yes.

237
00:14:06,833 --> 00:14:10,457
I'm still technically half-animal by
nature, so I can understand what they say.

238
00:14:10,540 --> 00:14:11,897
You can talk to animals?

239
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:13,320
Oh, wow, Chopper.

240
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:17,737
Between your medical skills and talking to
animals, you've got some amazing talents.

241
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:18,740
Don't be silly.

242
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:22,417
You jerk-flattering me like that isn't
going to make me happy or anything.

243
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:23,676
He sure looks happy.

244
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:26,937
Hey, what did you mean about
Chopper's medical skills anyway?

245
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:30,800
Well, Chopper here is a doctor
and a first-rate one at that. Dr.

246
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:34,528
Kureha taught him everything
there is to know about medicine.

247
00:14:34,700 --> 00:14:35,530
Impossible.

248
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:37,557
Chopper, are you seriously a doctor?

249
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:39,617
How cool. No way.

250
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:41,757
Really, Luffy, if you didn't know that,

251
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:44,257
what did you think Chopper was
when you asked him to join us?

252
00:14:44,340 --> 00:14:46,693
A talking transforming reindeer monster.

253
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:47,950
Backup food.

254
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:50,830
Wait, oh no!

255
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:53,937
I was in such a big hurry, I
left my medical bag behind.

256
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,257
It had all of my tools in it.

257
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:56,170
Your bag?

258
00:14:56,253 --> 00:14:57,099
But isn't this it?

259
